$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081759} {:answer/id #uuid "7d64ae0b-9e46-59e2-a92c-60495d5b9664" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.75$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081760}] :answer-field/id #uuid "408f5d83-6e23-56b4-a4bb-2d2ef4643f69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081755}] :question/id #uuid "53321164-8a61-5383-b3a2-e56b310063a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-5497" :question/problem "Consider the following game featuring an unfair coin. If the coin lands on heads, the player wins $\\$3$. If the coin lands on tails, the player loses $\\$1$. The unfair coin has the following probabilities:\n$P(Heads) = \\frac{3}{5}, P(Tails) = \\frac{2}{5}$.\nWhat is the expected profit at each toss in this game?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e6330530-50c5-51e9-b616-2b97ce42cade" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Decay Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3495ebe4-0ff8-587e-946b-39cf32f7c349" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$355$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348920} {:answer/id #uuid "585d5ff7-c990-5b8e-9c9c-dbc4951b081f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$586$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349258} {:answer/id #uuid "647c1398-390e-5363-ba09-9403a7d4d31e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$125$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349368} {:answer/id #uuid "b77d1897-d9d4-571e-809b-923026590486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$216$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350070} {:answer/id #uuid "bb175228-e457-5110-b2df-5ff95ab0825b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$966$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350110}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "585d5ff7-c990-5b8e-9c9c-dbc4951b081f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$586$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349258} :answer-field/id #uuid "2564adfc-5914-509e-b0ca-e7985013c023" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6894d124-282d-5217-8531-e4a1976ca68b" :question/math-academy-id "q-83140" :question/problem "The outstanding amount $L(t)$ that Daphne needs to repay the bank $t$ years after taking out a loan can be modeled by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.5L.\n$$\n\nIf she borrowed $\\$32\\,000,$ calculate the debt remaining after $8$ years. Round your answer to the nearest dollar." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "We model the amount of debt remaining using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}L}{\\text{d}t}=-0.5L.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nL(t)={L}_{0}\\,{e}^{-0.5t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${L}_{0}$ is the initial value.\n\nWe're told that $\\$32\\,000$ were borrowed, so we have ${L}_{0}=32\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the amount of debt $L$ remaining at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nL(t)=32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5t}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the amount of debt remaining when $t=8,$ we substitute $t=8$ into the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(8) & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-0.5\\cdot 8} \\\\  & =32\\,000\\,{e}^{-4} \\\\  & ≈586.100\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding our answer to the nearest integer, we conclude that $586$ dollars of debt remain."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088421 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0ba25c0c-9ba9-586a-b66f-7f07076d2827" :knowledge-point/title "Solving an Exponential Growth Problem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bed0619c-b398-5e69-bc05-ed10de39c428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$313327$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186087180} 