account, for which she decides to withdraw $\\$40$ to buy some medicine. What was Susan's ending balance?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c30919c-c2b9-5e09-8512-98fcbe339564" :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing a Profit Function Given a Revenue and Cost Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90f204d-b5fd-50c9-ab8c-d8cb4b6222f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$156250$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098008} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa89751-aace-5bff-8bb1-c2be65a367eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$156.25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098009} {:answer/id #uuid "3890698e-9da5-50d0-90e0-2976d44146cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1562.50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098010} {:answer/id #uuid "528267c0-40f6-5940-8c8a-3fd9c93dea14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$15625$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098011} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4e06c1-7da4-5aba-bffb-7933e156cec1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$24000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098012}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6a6c8563-2fe7-548b-9f56-af11980f0e76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098007}] :question/id #uuid "b2f81aed-e4a0-5851-8bbd-4f190161eccf" :question/math-academy-id "q-119066" :question/problem "A sculptor spends $C(x) = 40x - 5x^{3} + 0.75x^{4}$ hundreds of dollars to produce $x$ units of a sculpture per month. The sculptor sells each sculpture for $\\$4000$. Given that the sculptor can produce between $1$ and $6$ units per month, what is the maximum monthly profit the sculpture can make?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101285 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d2b1036-0ea4-5fd1-bfed-885dcbae618b" :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing a Profit Function by Constructing a Revenue and Cost Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2487f2f-e020-5418-9b7d-d19a03ee9b71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$58$ per night" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099032} {:answer/id #uuid "38131884-7f4d-575f-a1e5-da00176efb74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$87$ per night" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099033} {:answer/id #uuid "4926a422-b3d8-5f99-add7-565dd4faffdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$117$ per night" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099034} {:answer/id #uuid "4d2cb67b-0174-56e2-9fa6-1bd299fc4b73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$68$ per night" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099035} {:answer/id #uuid "6a0fc874-1268-525b-8150-c7a1418d576f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$93$ per night" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099036}] :answer-field/id #uuid "96d773bc-e220-5a77-ad6a-d1f876c3dabf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186099031}] :question/id #uuid "9ce65a44-c25d-58ff-9d3a-64a6416853bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-18673" :question/problem "A hotel has $50$ rooms. The manager observes that when the room rate is $\\$30$ per night, all rooms are occupied and, for every $\\$3$ increase in the rate, a single room is vacated. If the maintenance per rented room is $\\$6$ per night, what room rate should the manager set to obtain the maximum profit?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101504 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c30919c-c2b9-5e09-8512-98fcbe339564" :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing a Profit Function Given a Revenue and Cost Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17aa9f4f-ce84-554a-bc96-221077334d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$243\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510834} {:answer/id #uuid "933d6611-667a-577f-a7e0-6fa58e2da1ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$176\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511084} {:answer/id #uuid "9974f26a-f280-5eb2-933d-048ae35c522b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$310\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511101} {:answer/id #uuid "d8c2b6a7-709f-5948-a5f8-ebe843858f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$107\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511227} {:answer/id #uuid "ddbf2bc7-cb32-5dcc-bad6-c8c2e13465b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$200\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511240}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17aa9f4f-ce84-554a-bc96-221077334d69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$243\\,000.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510834} :answer-field/id #uuid "8efadd76-a965-516a-bd05-82f7d6c9e07e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100185}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f5c03e3f-902a-5f23-a083-877f778bea41" :question/math-academy-id "q-65867" :question/problem "A factory spends $C(x)={x}^{4}+13x$ thousand dollars to manufacture $x$ units of a certain product. The factory sells the product for $\\$121\\,000$ per unit. What is the maximum monthly profit that the factory can make given that it can produce at most $4$ items per month?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we apply the candidates test.\n\nFirst, note that for selling $x$ units of the product per month, the factory has a monthly revenue (income) of $R(x)=121\\cdot x=121x$ thousand dollars. \n\nTherefore, the profit function (in thousands of dollars) is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =R(x)-C(x) \\\\  & =121x-({x}^{4}+13x) \\\\  & =108x-{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe note that the permitted domain is $0\\le x\\le 4.$ Therefore, $x=0$ and $x=4$ are both candidates for the global maxima of $P(x).$\n\nWe need to find the critical points of $P(x)$ for $0<x<4.$ Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(x)=108-4{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand solving ${P}^{′}(x)=0$ gives the following critical point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 108-4{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{3} & =27 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAll that's left now is to confirm that $x=3$ does indeed give a maximum value of $P(x).$ To do this, we compute the second derivative:\n\n$$\n{P}^{″}(x)=-12{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating ${P}^{″}(x)$ at the critical point, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{″}(3)=-12(3)^{2}=-108<0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich confirms that $x=3$ is a maximum of $P(x).$ \n\nOur candidates are $x=0,$ $x=3$ and $x=4.$ Computing $P(x)$ at each of these values, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0) & =108(0)-{0}^{4}=0 \\\\ P(3) & =108(3)-{3}^{4}=243\\,✓ \\\\ P(4) & =108(4)-{4}^{4}=176\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the maximum monthly profit is $\\$243\\,000.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c30919c-c2b9-5e09-8512-98fcbe339564" :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing a Profit Function Given a Revenue and Cost Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc079cff-d7da-5a87-b324-3586bd45da20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$850$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100546} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a0efd8-50ec-59dd-9e81-0c4bfa6eebc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$640$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100547} {:answer/id #uuid "d055eaa7-a9f5-5d9e-932a-3b0feca2a7ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$483.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100548} {:answer/id #uuid "f8616558-a163-56ed-b4e0-530b461b2845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$219.7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100550} {:answer/id #uuid "5dffbfce-f42c-5aa6-9041-b83e50fdad63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dffbfce-f42c-5aa6-9041-b83e50fdad63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1\\,000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510979} :answer-field/id #uuid "66e4fa29-0429-5e20-b824-7bf28e1113c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186100545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e5396c61-6040-5997-8775-94633d636485" :question/math-academy-id "q-87573" :question/problem "A computer science center organizes a machine learning course. The course is activated if there are at least $3$ participants, and it can be attended by at most $13$ participants. The price for each participant is $\\$200.$ The cost of providing the course is $C(x)=200x-4{x}^{3}+0.3{x}^{4},$ where $x$ is the number of participants. What is the maximum profit that the computer science center can make?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we apply the candidates' test.\n\nFirst, note that for $x$ participants, the computer science center has a revenue (income) of $R(x)=200\\cdot x=200x$ dollars. \n\nTherefore, the profit function is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x) & =R(x)-C(x) \\\\  & =200x-(200x-4{x}^{3}+0.3{x}^{4}) \\\\  & =4{x}^{3}-0.3{x}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe note that the permitted domain is $3\\le x\\le 13.$ Therefore, $x=3$ and $x=13$ are candidates for the global maxima of $P(x).$\n\nWe need to find the critical points of $P(x)$ for $3\\ge x\\ge 13.$ Taking the derivative, we get\n\n$$\n{P}^{′}(x)=12{x}^{2}-1.2{x}^{3},\n$$\n\nand solving ${P}^{′}(x)=0$ gives the following critical points:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{′}(x) & =0 \\\\ 12{x}^{2}-1.2{x}^{3} & =0 \\\\ 1.2{x}^{2}(10-x) & =0 \\\\ x & =0,10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the critical points are $x=0$ and $x=10.$ However, the values $x=0$ is not in the permitted domain, so the only possible new candidate is $x=10.$\n\nLet's check if $x=10$ gives a maximum value of $P(x).$ To do this, we compute the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{″}(x) & =24x-3.6{x}^{2} \\\\ {P}^{″}(10) & =240-360=-120<0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second derivative at  $x=10$ is negative, the point $x=10$ is a maximum. \n\nOur candidates are $x=3,x=10$ and $x=13.$ Computing $P(x)$ at each of these values, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(3) & =4(3)^{3}-0.3(3)^{4}=83.7 \\\\ P(10) & =4(10)^{3}-0.3(10)^{4}=1\\,000\\,✓ \\\\ P(13) & =4(13)^{3}-0.3(13)^{4}=219.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the maximum profit is $\\$1\\,000.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106045 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e266bf6f-4cff-54e7-b474-4b5133ee2d12" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Feasible Region"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a55a0568-b351-5ca5-9708-9147c9a617b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102157} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d146b7-313d-5da7-9499-1b9da601e4a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$8400$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102158} {:answer/id #uuid "cd10c121-77e4-5255-a4e2-aff3d1de737a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$6500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102159} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a91e1f-bcf0-5e7b-999f-d96ece7e6302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The farmer can't fulfill the order" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102160} {:answer/id #uuid "f251ee55-58f8-54bd-b559-32832213c1ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102161}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ab6cdb20-50dd-52ce-8d3e-d8af17e85eeb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/typ