purchased is modeled by the function $V(t) = 1000 \\cdot (0.8)^{t}$. Calculate $V(4)$, and determine its meaning in this context.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e026db-b6ca-5d1f-bc3c-3be6b14dd14a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1.80$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116735} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf356cf-15b6-5092-9788-e98b4f596935" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$8.50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116736} {:answer/id #uuid "d22f8719-b0f3-5d7a-8f03-f8cb18846173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116737} {:answer/id #uuid "f581f57c-328a-511b-adf3-7882b27f3560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.02$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116738} {:answer/id #uuid "35dc34cf-6ed5-588b-8665-51cdf9e08eda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$6.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d22f8719-b0f3-5d7a-8f03-f8cb18846173" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116737} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3ac18f-df2a-531e-80f1-3bbd339896a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9fb6d92-70dd-5c7f-9979-070fe590bd5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107738" :question/problem "A bar of chocolate in the form of a rectangular prism is $9\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $2\\,\\text{cm}$ high. If the chocolate costs $\\$0.02$ per cubic centimeter, what is the value of four identical bars of chocolate?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of the bar of chocolate.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=5,\\,h=2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 5\\cdot 2=90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe total volume of the four bars of chocolate is\n\n$$\n90\\cdot 4=360\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the cost of four chocolate bars is\n\n$$\n360\\cdot 0.02=$7.20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfd31821-0cd4-55b3-bf7b-348b1cda26c5" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Initial Values and End Behavior"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a430732-d629-5671-bd74-e5753212fea8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$150$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128186} {:answer/id #uuid "bb07f46a-f6f8-5a0a-8b5f-a08acbe115e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$15$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128187} {:answer/id #uuid "cff08a88-4d98-53e9-b038-eb7422d53e16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128188} {:answer/id #uuid "f514e006-a686-507d-8daa-4fd052334128" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128189} {:answer/id #uuid "003884e7-06fe-5c2f-9dd2-a107c3140fe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128190}] :answer-field/id #uuid "88adfaf2-76a5-5dc1-b403-91b329e2dd15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128185}] :question/id #uuid "2318fb08-589b-5db1-abb5-74802350258b" :question/math-academy-id "q-45472" :question/problem "![](images/65/65ad8a8ac5c51a3ad54a621aafb8636b9f4cb6ec257f28003ce69322268eccb2.png)\n\nThe price $P(t)$, in tens of dollars, of a rare baseball card increases exponentially with time $t$, in years. The graph of $P$ is shown above. What was the initial price of the card according to the graph?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cfd31821-0cd4-55b3-bf7b-348b1cda26c5" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting Initial Values and End Behavior"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "beed2c29-f44d-58da-b332-d1411b727b07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$6000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128198} {:answer/id #uuid "bf450aaf-efd2-550f-8dd3-70754e522712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$14$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128199} {:answer/id #uuid "c951df84-865e-5709-8f4a-21af8a4a0401" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128200} {:answer/id #uuid "26e697c2-2421-5302-ac43-64c4dac238f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$14000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128201} {:answer/id #uuid "2f9bdac7-1057-53af-8779-184d5675e036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128202}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e19929d4-597c-5f95-adbe-78e32c50230f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128197}] :question/id #uuid "7831e92e-44dd-53c9-919f-fe817b80ee19" :question/math-academy-id "q-45653" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8eb234b3a2cced80f847f88ff675bbbea87e2e2b402444df726143e324e2650e.png)\n\nThe value of a particular car can be modeled using an exponential function $P(t)$. The quantity $P$ is measured in thousands of dollars, and $t$ is the time, in years, since the car was first manufactured. The graph of $P(t)$ is shown above. Find an approximate value for the car $24$ years after it was first manufactured."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fd286741-bf82-5723-a9c1-acf7a8b238c2" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Least-Squares Regression Line in Context"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9949e4b7-78dc-54e1-b1e2-6cc17d5fdb53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132212} {:answer/id #uuid "bdfe35c5-c31d-517c-8491-ee60cd035209" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$10400$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132213} {:answer/id #uuid "ed8de521-183c-5b4c-8a34-a2af3d37fe8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$12200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132214} {:answer/id #uuid "0e37fc32-c14e-5987-8701-bf2b47456c68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$11500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132215} {:answer/id #uuid "3f07dfd0-be79-5868-bcec-3c18ae2a9bd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$11300$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132216}] :answer-field/id #uuid "891df652-ad00-5c9b-a50d-52740ac80a98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132211} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "481e34c4-8e23-5638-8364-a626e241a934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$10\\,400$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370921} {:answer/id #uuid "f52f14f2-3d6a-50fd-9ea7-988fb8ad0119" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$12\\,200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370922} {:answer/id #uuid "bedb7f6d-404b-5d77-ac8f-a59e15f52f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$11\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370923} {:answer/id #uuid "d21b58ed-a896-595c-927e-75a0413683ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9\\,200$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370924} {:answer/id #uuid "e75bad89-4049-573b-b220-b46d90025c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$11\\,300$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e75bad89-4049-573b-b220-b46d90025c2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$11\\,300$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370925} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5153227-95be-5d76-8614-6897e17ccc0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "378d2a03-3c23-5c86-9c0e-a7a3f421ff89" :question/math-academy-id "q-41742" :question/problem "A store collected data about its profits (in thousands of dollars) for the first five months since opening. This data is shown below.\n\n\n\n<div class=\"source-table-scroll\"><table class=\"source-table\" data-rules=\"all\" data-table-align=\"center\" data-frame=\"true\">\n<tbody><tr data-next-row=\"true\">\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Month $(x)$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$1$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$2$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$3$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$4$</strong></td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\"><strong>$5$</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<th data-cell-align=\"center\" data-fill=\"#D6EAF8\">Profit $(y)$</th>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$8.3$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$5.1$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10.9$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$10.7$</td>\n<td data-cell-align=\"center\">$9.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n\n\nFind the line of the form $y={\\beta }_{0}+{\\beta }_{1}x$ that best fits the data above. According to the model, what will be the profit in the $6$th month, assuming that the trend continues?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that*\n\n$$\n({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}=\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{X}^{T}y=\\begin{bmatrix}44.5 \\\\ 141.5\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n*where $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $y$ is the observation vector.*" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The coefficients of the line that best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution $\\hat{\\beta }$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}}^{X}\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1}\\end{bmatrix}}^{\\beta } & =\\overbrace{\\begin{bmatrix}8.3 \\\\ 5.1 \\\\ 10.9 \\\\ 10.7 \\\\ 9.5\\end{bmatrix}}^{y},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\beta $ is the parameter vector, and $y$ is the observation vector.\n\nPre-multiplying this equation by ${X}^{T},$ we obtain the corresponding normal equation\n\n$$\n{X}^{T}\\,X\\hat{\\beta }={X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $X$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${X}^{T}X$ is invertible and \n\n$$\n\\hat{\\beta }=({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}y.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given values of $({X}^{T}X)^{-1}$ and ${X}^{T}y$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{\\beta } & =({X}^{T}\\,X)^{-1}{X}^{T}\\,y \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}11 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}44.5 \\\\ 141.5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6.5 \\\\ 0.8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the line $y=6.5+0.8x.$\n\nFinally, to predict the profit in the $6$th month, we substitute $x=6$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =6.5+0.8(6) \\\\  & =11.3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, according to the model, the profit in the $6$th month will be $\\$11\\,300.$\n\n**Note**: Since we're extrapolating ($x=6$ is not within the range of the original set of $x$-values), our result *may* be unreliable."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ad5ad311-bf6f-58e9-a473-51ad651160fd" :knowledge-poi