"$$3350000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174018} {:answer/id #uuid "fcb19fe8-0132-5915-b6ab-20803dc425fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2950000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174019} {:answer/id #uuid "3f16607e-ab5b-5330-bd25-2c1cc0069e03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2250000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174020} {:answer/id #uuid "75656849-d4f0-5fb4-9e7e-be213ce44d66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4450000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174021}] :answer-field/id #uuid "62e0ea1b-8bc2-5645-8cb5-11acf72aeb0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174016}] :question/id #uuid "e856ef79-2401-51e5-bdf8-06c6ab15323e" :question/math-academy-id "q-116355" :question/problem "The cost, $C(x)$, and revenue, $R(x)$, functions, in hundreds of dollars, of a large company are\n$$\n\\displaystyle C(x) = 2500 + 50x, R(x) = 250x - 0.25x^{2},\n$$\nwhere $x$ denotes the number of units sold per month. What is the maximum profit that the company can make per month?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176340 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0286d36b-217f-52e4-8580-e031b6dea31e" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Residuals Using the Regression Line Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b7198df-fc16-57b1-a77a-b9edff234f9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174302} {:answer/id #uuid "640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554063} {:answer/id #uuid "66ae108f-494f-57ed-a796-8e17686429c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$(-2\\,500)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554072} {:answer/id #uuid "6bb39097-7715-5a68-b897-b0f54a11856e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554080} {:answer/id #uuid "844c502d-5d46-511c-9e11-95d3245ec04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$(-1\\,500)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "640b6612-5cd5-5b2b-b186-165710224e82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2\\,500$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186554063} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd589229-6d62-561a-8ccf-4b0128261c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174298}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a189cf42-a35d-541c-8fa9-b13012c26ed3" :question/math-academy-id "q-134266" :question/problem "An antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $x$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The equation of the corresponding linear regression line for this data is \n\n$$\ny=3.2x+4.5.\n$$\n\nWhat is the residual $5$ decades after the artwork was produced if the actual value of the artwork after $5$ decades is $\\$23\\,000?$" :question/worked-solution "The residual equals the difference between the actual value of the dependent variable and the value estimated using the linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\text{Residual}=\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated}\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we compute the estimated value using our linear regression model:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\widehat{y} & =3.2x+4.5 \\\\  & =3.2(5)+4.5 \\\\  & =20.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Residual} & =\\text{Actual}-\\text{Estimated} \\\\  & =y-\\widehat{y} \\\\  & =23-20.5 \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the residual is $\\$2\\,500.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e77a14c-9943-5494-ae89-a77c7a1888d0" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Residuals From a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a774593d-dc82-5d50-8667-fb9ab35ab5db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$(-10000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174311} {:answer/id #uuid "be631636-35f9-5288-8344-819217c75758" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$5000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174312} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a353ec-507e-5e8c-a1d6-f5c33eae2784" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$(-5000)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174313} {:answer/id #uuid "fac8b2f2-21e2-5ba4-9832-76e2f12eff72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$10000$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174314} {:answer/id #uuid "7a22e90f-667d-50ab-9770-629412ff6774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174315}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6dc00c1c-9fd6-5d82-925a-2adc1e918fcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186174310}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e312e8e0-12d2-524c-8d6c-c3bb62aee103" :question/math-academy-id "q-134276" :question/problem "![](images/15/15d2ded66d86366f481f5e88e3b45fbfc7e4d227b9f49aee35797554412fbb87.png)\n\nAn antique broker has records about the value of an artwork $y$ (in thousands of dollars) at certain times $t$ (in decades) since the artwork was produced. The scatter plot for the data and the corresponding linear regression line are shown above.\n\nAccording to the regression model, what is the residual for the highlighted datapoint?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176492 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a73e128-df8b-5f7b-bf88-4b5c584c27a5" :knowledge-point/title "Maximizing Profit and Revenue Functions, and Minimizing Cost Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f49ed4a-d1c5-5072-936c-